---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<Base title="PhD Research">
  <section class="frame tight" style="padding-top: var(--sp-5);">
    <div class="grid-margin">
      <div class="margin-col">PhD research<br/>UC Santa Cruz<br/>2025&ndash;present</div>
      <div>
        <h1 class="page-title">How vehicle inertia shapes wind estimation</h1>

        <p class="dek" style="margin-top: var(--sp-3); max-width: 560px;">
          My M.S. work measured wind directly. This work estimates it indirectly &mdash;
          from how a multirotor's own motion responds to the air around it. Prior work
          shows that estimation accuracy improves with model fidelity, and that aircraft
          more sensitive to aerodynamic drag give better estimates of time-varying wind.
          That creates a tradeoff: heavier vehicles respond more slowly, but need higher
          rotor speeds to hover, which increases drag sensitivity. This project asks which
          effect wins.
        </p>

        <h3 style="margin-top: var(--sp-4);">Three ways in</h3>

        <div style="margin-top: var(--sp-2);">
          <p class="subhead">Software-in-the-loop simulation</p>
          <p class="dek" style="max-width: 560px;">
            Characterizes vehicle-level dynamic response across a range of simulated
            inertia configurations, using broadband excitation and system identification
            to compare model bandwidth as mass changes.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div style="margin-top: var(--sp-3);">
          <p class="subhead">Wind tunnel testing</p>
          <p class="dek" style="max-width: 560px;">
            At the UC Davis Atmospheric Boundary Layer Wind Tunnel, propeller drag is
            characterized across combinations of rotor speed, wind speed and turbulence
            intensity &mdash; measuring aerodynamic loads, current, voltage, PWM command and
            propeller speed.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div style="margin-top: var(--sp-3);">
          <p class="subhead">Flight validation</p>
          <p class="dek" style="max-width: 560px;">
            Real flight tests vary vehicle mass by adding weight in the battery bay,
            keeping airframe geometry and center of mass nearly unchanged, to confirm
            the simulated trends hold in practice.
          </p>
        </div>

        <h3 style="margin-top: var(--sp-4);">Early results</h3>
        <p style="margin-top: var(--sp-2); max-width: 560px;">
          Across a 2.5&ndash;5.5 kg mass range on a quadcopter platform, plunge damping
          decreases monotonically as mass increases &mdash; meaning heavier vehicles are
          less translationally responsive, as expected. Wind tunnel characterization also
          confirmed a spanwise turbulence-intensity gradient in the test section, suitable
          for studying propeller response under varying inflow.
        </p>

        <div class="rule-sm"></div>

        <p class="eyebrow">
          Accepted for AIAA SciTech 2027. Full bandwidth analysis and flight-validation
          results are in progress &mdash; see <a href={`${base}publications/`}>publications</a> for
          the latest version.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
